Hi,

I have now got a permanent call-in number at InstantConference.com it is 
also free of charge for the Linux Foundation (not toll-free for calling 
in from the US), but in contrary to Freeconferencecall.com this number 
will not expire. Recording is available also free of charge, to be 
controlled from the phone keypad or via a web interface. After the 
conference call finishes, an MP3 file gets generated which I can 
download from their web interface and upload on one of our web servers. 
It is also possible to turn of the music in the time until the second 
caller arrives. So we can use this number also for providing call-in 
services to our face-to-face meetings. I can also order more access 
codes for free to get call-in to several rooms in parallel.

The number shown below will be the principal call-in number for 
OpenPrinting, general phone meetings, preparation meetings for 
face-to-face meetings, and call-in to face-to-face meetings.

If no one objects this will also be the call-in number for OpenPrinting 
